5.16\",\"35.504\",\"1,739.656\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JWTY1R161S033FC\",\"t\":\"Pacific Biochar\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.2\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.2\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.1\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWTY1R161S033FC/prj_1JXCRW5ST1S0EEKH/pjd_1K8XQYT1E1S0VMCZ/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 31 Oct 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KT245NCR1S0AHXQ?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWTY1R161S033FC/prj_1JXCRW5ST1S0EEKH/pjd_1KSHNFFMC1S0DJ1Z/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWTY1R161S033FC/prj_1JXCRW5ST1S0EEKH/pjd_1KSHNEXVF1S0SX6A/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWTY1R161S033FC/prj_1JXCRW5ST1S0EEKH/pjd_1KPXX0RXK1S0PJAV/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWTY1R161S033FC/prj_1JXCRW5ST1S0EEKH/pjd_1KPXWZPCE1S0F8KH/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWTY1R161S033FC/prj_1JXCRW5ST1S0EEKH/pjd_1KM6AWYT01S0S0VY/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n200Y+\\nHumboldt Sawmill Company (HSC)\\nPacific Biochar\\nISSUED\\n6,967.97\\nBUFFER POOL\\n139.363\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Jun 2025 to 31 May 2030\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nPacific Biochar specializes in the production and distribution of high-quality biochar products designed to sequester carbon while enhancing agricultural and industrial productivity. Pacific Biochar utilizes existing biomass power plant infrastructure to produce biochar, enabling rapid scaling potential with low capital investments. The partnerships we make with these bioenergy facilities result in cascading community benefits including wildfire risk reduction, rural job growth, and improved food security. Biochar production, located in Scotia, CA with annual credit production of ~10,600 tCO2e/year\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nHD88\\nApproval date\\n16 Dec 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.2\\nBaseline protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.1\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nHumboldt Sawmill Company (HSC)\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n31 Oct 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 708.66 tCO₂e removed from Humboldt Sawmill Company (HSC) on 30 Apr 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n708.663 t\\nSequestrations\\n740.990 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n32.328 tCO₂e\\n+\\nCounterfactuals\\n0 kgCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n26 May 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n26 May 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n23 Apr 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n23 Apr 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n20 Mar 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 12\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n6,967.97\\nRetired\\n3,199.354\\nBuffer pool\\n139.363\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jun 2025 to 31 May 2030\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n26 Jun 2026\\t708.66\\t14.174\\t694.486\\n26 May 2026\\t759.59\\t15.192\\t744.398\\n23 Apr 2026\\t575.07\\t11.502\\t563.568\\n20 Mar 2026\\t519.25\\t10.385\\t508.865\\n20 Mar 2026\\t803.84\\t16.078\\t787.762\\n30 Jan 2026\\t559.25\\t11.185\\t548.065\\n16 Dec 2025\\t1,267.15\\t25.343\\t1,241.807\\n16 Dec 2025\\t1,775.16\\t35.504\\t1,739.656\\nShowing 8 of 8\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Pacific Biochar's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 139.363 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 139.363 certificates.\\n\\nPacific Biochar has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"